            "title": "Pearl Avenue Teens Reach Meeting",
            "description": "<p>Teens Reach is the youth council for the San José Public Library, providing a key way for young adults to build their leadership skills by developing and participating in library activities, as well as becoming library advisors and advocates.</p>\n<p>For ages 13-18.</p>\n<p>Pearl Avenue's&nbsp;Teens Reach group meets monthly on&nbsp;the third Thursday with&nbsp;socializing and fun at 4:00 pm.<br></p>\n<p>Our in-person meet up plans include:<br></p>\n<ul><li>Teen Volunteer Opportunities</li><li>Election for Advisory Board</li><li>Community Youth&nbsp;Engagement</li><li>Games & Activities</li><li>Snacks</li><li>Guest Speakers</li></ul>\n<p>Bring a friend, and learn more about what to expect with volunteering this year.<br></p>\n<p>If you are new to volunteering with the San Jose Public Library, please visit the <a href=\"https://www.sjpl.org/teensreach?_gl=1*1xw75jd*_ga*MTc0Mzc1MDkxNi4xNTk1ODc5Nzg5*_ga_G99DMMNG39*MTcxMDQ2MjAyNC4zMDIuMS4xNzEwNDYzNzYzLjAuMC4w*_ga_F5QPDQX1BM*MTcxMDQ2MjAyNC4zMDEuMS4xNzEwNDYzNzYyLjAuMC4w\">Teens Reach: Community Service</a> webpage&nbsp;or more information and be sure to create your online volunteer account (click “Sign Me Up” under Pearl Avenue Branch).<br><br></p>\n<p><a href=\"https://www.sjpl.org/ada-event-accommodation/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" data-auth=\"NotApplicable\" title=\"https://www.sjpl.org/ada-event-accommodation/\" data-linkindex=\"6\">ADA Accommodation Requests</a></p>\n<p><em></em></p>\n<p></p>",
